  "Healthy negatives are the calibration year's shared calendar holdout; no independent healthy negative exists on any LBNL system (D2). Per-day autocorrelation makes any binomial p on these counts optimistic.",
  "The model- and device-conformance thresholds are quantile-calibrated on these same holdout days (fpr_quantile); for those two channels the holdout-FP row is the calibration target, not an out-of-sample measurement. No healthy data unseen by every calibration step exists.",
